Error [E0201]: `item` cannot be moved from borrowed storage
  --> tests/ui/copy_out_payload_in_place.jet:44:39
    |
 44 |     loop item in items -> &sink.push(^item)
    |                                       ^^^^
 Why: `item` reads its value through a view of the place it was bound to, so that place keeps the value; moving it here would copy it
 Fix: Write `item.copy()` when `.push()` should receive a copy, or move the place itself with `^` when this scope owns it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0201

